# Reloads no longer free event objects that live creatures still point to.
#  1. Creature events: Creature::eventsList holds raw pointers into CreatureEvents' map. After a reload of creaturescripts,
#     scripts or everything, CreatureEvents::removeInvalidEvents() erased every entry left without a script (an XML
#     event whose file now fails to load or was removed, a revscript that no longer registers it) while logged-in players
#     and spawned monsters still held it, and it went on with the erased iterator. The next think / kill / death /
#     health change / extended opcode / modal window ... of such a creature read freed memory (AddressSanitizer:
#     heap-use-after-free in Creature::getCreatureEvents). Now nothing is erased: an event without a script stays in the
#     map, unloaded (getCreatureEvents and the global login / logout / advance loops skip it), and a later reload that
#     brings the script back reuses the same object, so it works again for the creatures that hold it. An event whose name
#     comes back with another type is moved out of the map but kept alive (never freed). The execute functions return
#     at once for an unloaded event (a reload run from inside an event, e.g. the admin panel's "Reload system" from an
#     extended opcode, can unload the events after it in the list being walked).
#  2. Monster spells: a monster attack / defense that names a registered spell (spells.xml or a revscript Spell) keeps a
#     pointer into Spells' maps. A reload of scripts (or everything) frees the revscript spells and the SIGHUP reload
#     reloads spells after monsters; monster types made by scripts are not in a monsters reload at all. The next cast
#     used freed memory (Monster::doAttacking). The block now keeps the spell's name and Monsters::updateSpellLinks()
#     points it at the spell registered under that name after every reload that clears spells (none: the block is skipped).
# Actions, movements, talkactions, globalevents and weapons are looked up at each use; nothing keeps their pointers.
# Apply in the server source root after 0001-0011: patch -p1 < 0012-reload-keeps-live-event-pointers.patch, then rebuild.
